        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The form, taken apart — source boundary",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Punjabi University Patiala's lexical statistics identifies ਹੁੰਦਾ (hundaa) as the masculine singular non-perfect form of ਹੋ, with continuous or habitual use. Its reference grammar gives ਹੋ as the stem of ਹੋਣਾ and lists ਹੁੰਦਾ (hundaa) as Present II. Punjabi University lesson 13 describes the agreeing -dā construction with a present auxiliary, and its verb reference identifies ਹੈ as the third-person singular present auxiliary. Sources: Punjabi University lexical statistics, Punjabi University reference grammar, Punjabi University lesson 13, and Punjabi University verb reference."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Those sources support the modern form. Reuse the history already attached to ਹੋਣਾ; do not invent a second etymology for an inflected form. This chapter teaches the habitual reading only, not generic “is,” a progressive, counterfactual “would,” a past form, or a feminine or plural form."
            }
          ]
        },
